# Intent: The on-unit face detector (owner brief 2026-11-17), experiment image only (CONFIG_MAIPAI_FACE_DETECT). maipai_facedet_core.h is the pure part a host compiler tests: fd_convert_rgb888 turns a window of the camera frame (YUYV, UYVY, RGB565 little endian or gray, BT.601) into the RGB888 the face models take, with an optional red/blue swap for a channel order check; fd_crop_origin places the 160 by 120 window (centered on a point, kept inside the frame, even column); fd_pick chooses the one face (the largest weighted toward the middle, above the score floor); fd_ring_t and fd_percentile give the p50 and p99 of the measured milliseconds; fd_period_ms clamps the rate to 2 to 5 a second; fd_model_parse names the models. maipai_facedet.cc is the device side: one task (priority 1 on core 0, a 12 KB stack in PSRAM, never touches flash, NVS or a partition: the model is read in place from the app image, the library's partition code is not on that path) that is created lazily on the first call and does nothing until asked. Per frame it asks for the camera-on cue (1.2 s, before every grab), takes the unit's own camera frame through the new StackChanCamera::DetectGrab (same lock, same two-read rule and the same 150 KB copy that is freed at once as SeekGrab), converts the window into a PSRAM RGB buffer (the conversion time is measured apart), and runs the model: MSR plus MNP (primary; on the whole 320 by 240 frame, the library shrinks it to 120 by 160) or ESPDet-Pico 224 (on a 160 by 120 native crop, in the middle or around the last face), selectable by the Kconfig default and per call. The model is created at the first run (weights copied to PSRAM, activations in PSRAM, max_internal_size 0, greedy manager), is refused when internal RAM is under the admission floor (the bench can force it), prints the library's profile_memory table once per load, and is freed 10 s after the last use. The newest face (center, size, score, the picture's time, a sequence number) is published under a spinlock; maipai_fd_want keeps a detection stream running at the configured rate only while a caller renews it (it stops within 1 s of the last renewal and never reads the camera with vision off, muted or in full quiet). No tool and no caller yet: FD03 adds the bench tools, FD04 the tracker.
# Placement: unit (carve-out 3, the robot turns toward a face with no brain; only a box, a score and a time exist, no picture is kept and no identity is made)
# Upstream: new firmware/main/hal/maipai_facedet_core.h, maipai_facedet.{h,cc}; firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_camera.{h,cc} (patches S13 and FI02). Library: espressif/esp-dl 3.3.15 and human_face_detect 0.5.2 (patch FD01)
# Check after a flash: nothing runs by itself; with FD03 on top: self.look.detect_test on the bench answers p50 and p99 times, the pixel format and the memory numbers, the camera cue is lit for every frame, the internal free before and after a model load and unload cycle matches within 1 KB, and the model's memory table appears once in the cable log.

